  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d438db151172ddd46b2e641cfe234f8a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LogManager
  allLogs:
  - id: FRAG_01
    text: "Galaxy: Milky Way\nid: 000024173\n\nThe fog eats sound. I threw a rock
      and never heard it land. My AI looped the same warning with different timestamps,
      then answered my descent-question with \u201CUnknown\u201D too fast. Something
      changed my fall mid-air. This isn\u2019t a first crash\u2014metal is buried
      under the moss like it\u2019s been happening for years."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2d9bcabd73184ac4da8099a7b04eb374, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Fog
  - id: FRAG_02
    text: "Galaxy: Milky Way\nid: 000024173\n\n\nMet Tamira. She wouldn\u2019t say
      \u201Cyes\u201D to other crash sites\u2014only, \u201CYou won\u2019t be the
      last.\u201D She looked at my wreck like she\u2019d seen the same scene before.
      If she\u2019s right, Aurelia isn\u2019t unlucky. It\u2019s consistent, and
      that\u2019s worse."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 37c6dcacc092ef44cba3e23193aa972b, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Tamira
  - id: FRAG_03
    text: "Galaxy: Milky Way\nid: 000024173\n\nLuminar Outpost is friendly in a practiced
      way.  Their leader speaks of \u201Crestoration\u201D like it\u2019s inevitable,
      and everyone nods on cue. I asked about repeated crashes\u2014got \u201CI don\u2019t
      know.\u201D Too clean. Like they\u2019ve rehearsed not knowing."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: af592e49a2fe41b48930ba7062794881, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Virelia Frontier
  - id: FRAG_04
    text: "Galaxy: Triangulum (M33)\nid: 000031902\n\nA field scholar blocked a scrap
      pile and escalated fast\u2014polite, annoyed, then possessive. He called it
      \u201Ca chapter of history,\u201D not metal. He touched it like it was sacred.
      Luminar doesn\u2019t just study relics\u2014they claim ownership. That kind
      of \u201Ccare\u201D turns into control."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 901bdfb5efb5d6144a090f1323f2da22, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Danriel
  - id: FRAG_05
    text: "Galaxy: Andromeda (M31)\nid: 000018447\n\nA yellow-sacked plant vents
      a fog that burns your throat and blurs vision. My visor flashed warning symbols
      my AI failed to translate\u2014twice.  Others breathed this poison and kept
      going. The planet\u2019s hazards feel like filters, not accidents."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c093f6d896bbfbd4f868e7e930634b95, type: 3}
    figureCaption: spore
  - id: FRAG_06
    text: 'Galaxy: Triangulum (M33)

      id: 000031902


      Harvel showed me
      runes etched into metal like the material carries instructions.. When I asked
      if runes could alter ship systems, he got too interested. If Aurelia ran on
      one regulated backbone system, the shutdown makes sense. '
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 47cf4617beaaa044ba03ed2bcbcad8e2, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Harvel
  - id: FRAG_07
    text: "Galaxy: Whirlpool (M51)\nid: 000052611\n\nRiftlands fog climbs uphill
      and shrinks the world to a few steps. Sound dies, then panic starts. There\u2019s
      an outpost in the rock above\u2014no smiles, no softness. A place like this
      trains people to distrust anything that arrives easily."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f0f8ba4269b6a2a48a19755f8b70f015, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Riftlands
  - id: FRAG_08
    text: "Galaxy: Andromeda (M31)\nid: 000018447\n\n\nEira didn\u2019t sell me hope.
      She gave commands: \u201CSit. Breathe. Tell the truth.\u201D. Luminar promises
      a future. Solace keeps you alive long enough to reach one. When you\u2019re
      scared, you can tell which is real."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ea2a6949e452ed649a3837bf7ebfbb0c, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Eira
  - id: FRAG_09
    text: "Galaxy: Andromeda (M31)\nid: 000018447\n\nErixa told me to keep anything
      with markings\u2014runes, stamps, warnings. \u201CSometimes it doesn\u2019t
      feel like scrap,\u201D she said. Like someone meant it to be found. If crashes
      are common, then messages are too."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 41335cb1e78031d4ba8b3fc5e98bab3f, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Erixa
  - id: FRAG_10
    text: "Galaxy: Milky Way\nid: 000024173\n\nMaerlon said ships don\u2019t just
      fall\u2014they get taken by \u201Csnares\u201D under the earth. I laughed. "
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d385a60c5b1f1fb4da715fcdeb81d66c, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Maerlon
  - id: FRAG_11
    text: Uniform stress scars suggest the system failed everywhere at once when
      the regulator collapsed. These segments are ideal as replacement conduits and
      frame supports for ship repairs
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b12caf66ef912334ab834515dc9750a6, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Pipe
  - id: FRAG_12
    text: "Lightweight composite metal with treated inner walls\u2014likely part
      of a regulated distribution network."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8cbce0a3a5429f14d9996229ea084683, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Metal piece
  - id: FRAG_13
    text: The unit has no obvious battery housing, implying it depended on constant
      regulated power.
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 39d70ad55eb2d6f488b1f7e04184c971, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Robot Arm
  - id: FRAG_14
    text: Salvage the chassis plating and couplers as durable housings for ship electronics.
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 54d3b794ff08ed04e9048c00f7d9d3eb, type: 3}
    figureCaption: helmet
  - id: FRAG_15
    text: "The unit has no obvious battery housing, implying it depended on constant
      regulated power. It died mid-task when the network collapsed\u2014single point
      of failure, planet-wide."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cc8ecae90398c9f41adc0871d949dc9c, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Robot
  - id: FRAG_16
    text: "This was an interface device, not a toy\u2014micro-etched runes form a
      calibration map that likely adapted to the wearer. It can\u2019t boot without
      the old power/regulation, but the optics and sensor band are intact. "
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 54d3b794ff08ed04e9048c00f7d9d3eb, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Headset
  - id: FRAG_17
    text: 'The alloy and etched logic grooves are useful both as scrap and as translation
      patterns. '
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a6d8053c43281e440aea98de951c623e, type: 3}
    figureCaption: sign
  - id: FRAG_18
    text: "Galaxy: Milky Way\nid: 000024173\n\nThe Archivist reads runes like they\u2019re
      listening for a pulse. They said \u201Cthe ones who built the heartbeat,\u201D
      then stopped mid-sentence. Their notes are out of order on purpose\u2014or
      because memory keeps slipping."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 26b44f74fb669444e88bba1bbc14791e, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Emerys
  - id: FRAG_19
    text: "Galaxy: Andromeda (M31)\nid: 000018447\n\nThe scrapper knows where metal
      lies and where it breaks clean. He said the old alloys feel dead until they
      don\u2019t\u2014like they remember force. When I asked about all the wrecks,
      he just said, \u201CThis place collects.\u201D"
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d745fde43aba34b48b5c3dfd84c8accb, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Grald
  - id: FRAG_20
    text: "Galaxy: Triangulum (M33)\nid: 000031902\n\nThe leader speaks warm, but
      the outpost listens like a machine. She calls the collapse a \u201Ctrial,\u201D
      not a mistake. People who say that usually plan to try again\u2014just cleaner."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 125ae0b4e88bad745bd3988417b22d13, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Sanya
  - id: FRAG_21
    text: "Galaxy: Whirlpool (M51)\nid: 000052611\n\nEvery record points to one \u201Cheartbeat\u201D
      powering the world. The historian got excited, then scared\u2014fast. When
      I asked where it is, she changed the subject too smoothly."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1a26ea13deeda1343a909e34cd698c30, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Julisa
  - id: FRAG_22
    text: "Galaxy: Pinwheel (M101)\nid: 000033800\n\nRiftlands doesn\u2019t welcome
      strangers. It measures them. Ash lines show where you stand, where you wait,
      where you don\u2019t cross. Fear here is organized."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 324256ec22148024a885bd2a44d3fa23, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Riftlands
  - id: FRAG_23
    text: "Galaxy: Large Magellanic Cloud\nid: 000077201\n\nA researcher drew the
      world like veins from a buried heart. \u201CWhen it stopped, everything died
      together,\u201D he said\u2014flat, practiced. That\u2019s what scares me most."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7552889033bf72c4c911f45a765c9cf4, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Kase
  - id: FRAG_24
    text: "Galaxy: Andromeda (M31)\nid: 000018447\n\nThe resource keeper counts everything,
      even people. Strangers are \u201Crisk\u201D in a column. He isn\u2019t cruel\u2014he\u2019s
      cornered by the mountain."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: fc2cb10a8c6751445b83c33f35fc203a, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Drayk
  - id: FRAG_25
    text: "Galaxy: Sombrero (M104)\nid: 000009413\n\nThe leader says the old machine
      made people soft, then made them dead. When I asked about ships falling, he
      didn\u2019t deny it. He said, \u201CNothing falls here by accident forever.\u201D"
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 354e6b382ca89f54d80016ff67c74c9a, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Marrek
  - id: FRAG_26
    text: "Galaxy: Milky Way\nid: 000024173\n\nA young scholar calls the ruins unfinished
      music. Maybe. But it\u2019s also a system that died mid-function. People talk
      about \u201Crestoring\u201D it and skip the part where it killed the world
      once."
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7fcd532bda4513f479d267b191985afc, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Camla
  - id: FRAG_27
    text: "Galaxy: Whirlpool (M51)\nid: 000052611\n\nI watched metal dust move the
      wrong way\u2014uphill, against wind, against gravity. Not fast. Just steady,
      like it was being reeled in. The fog thickened around it and my headset popped
      with static for one second, then cleared. "
    figureSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 08d126b514cc4bc4c957730869d61574, type: 3}
    figureCaption: Loose Metal
